## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                    ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                     ← composition root: wires every module here
├── config/env.ts              ← the only file that reads process.env
├── middlewares/                ← cross-cutting error / validation glue
├── shared/                     ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
├── core/                       ← business rules, zero framework dependencies
│   ├── entities/               ← domain entities
│   ├── ports/                  ← abstract interfaces (repository contracts)
│   └── use-cases/<module>/     ← one class per operation
└── adapters/<module>/          ← concrete implementations of core ports
    ├── controllers/            ← Koa ctx handlers
    ├── routes/                 ← route factories (bind HTTP verbs to controller methods)
    ├── presenters/             ← maps domain entities → API response shapes
    ├── dto/                    ← request validation schemas
    └── repositories/           ← ORM-specific repository implementations
```

Dependency rule: `adapters/` depends on `core/` — never the reverse.

